## How to cite

This repository ships a [CITATION.cff](CITATION.cff), so GitHub shows a
**“Cite this repository”** button and tools such as Zotero can import it.

BibTeX:

```bibtex
@misc{orthodox2000_ml10gen9_graphics_fix,
  author       = {Orthodox2000},
  title        = {HP ProLiant ML10 Gen9 --- Graphics / Display Fix
                  (Linux, Windows Server \& more)},
  year         = {2026},
  version      = {1.1.0},
  howpublished = {GitHub repository},
  url          = {https://github.com/Orthodox2000/ProLiant-ML10-Graphics-fix-Linux},
  note         = {MIT License}
}
```

Plain text:

> Orthodox2000. *HP ProLiant ML10 Gen9 — Graphics / Display Fix (Linux, Windows
> Server & more)*, version 1.1.0, 2026.
> https://github.com/Orthodox2000/ProLiant-ML10-Graphics-fix-Linux

## Contributors

If you tested this on another board, distribution or monitor, add yourself here
in your pull request. Contributions of any size are welcome.
